 "method": "CANDID (Gallenne et al. 2015) grid search on MIRC-X OIFITS (pipeline v1.3.3, ncoh=10, max integration 60 s; modified calibration using MIRC IDL routines). Detection search used closure phases only, out to 0.3 arcsec (grism-mode field of view). Primary UD diameter first fitted from closure phase + visibility and used for the UD single-star model. Detection threshold 5 sigma (CANDID n-sigma from chi2). On detection, CANDID rerun fitting separation, PA, both diameters, flux ratio and 'resolved flux' (6-parameter model); if only primary resolved, companion diameter fixed at 0.01 mas (5-parameter model). All five detections reached 8 sigma, the maximum CANDID permits. Detection limits: CANDID injection-recovery over the whole FOV; at each separation the highest flux ratio (over all PA) returning 5 sigma is taken; for detected systems the companion signal is removed first and limits derived on the residual closure phases. (Sect. 2.1-2.3, 3.1-3.2, pp.2-6.)",
 "flux_ratio_definition": "Table 3 caption: 'resolved flux and flux ratio in percent relative to the primary' (companion flux as a percentage of primary flux, in H band). Detection limits (Table 5) are in magnitudes (Delta H): 'highest flux ratio companion that CANDID can recover ... equivalent to a 5 sigma detection'.",
 "uncertainties": "Not stated explicitly as statistical vs systematic. Table 3 gives CANDID fit uncertainties (very small, e.g. +-0.007 mas in separation). The paper does not describe a systematic floor, calibration-error inflation or bootstrap. Text: 'Error bars [on companion frequency] are derived using the binomial distribution formalism of Burgasser et al. (2003)' (Sect. 3.3, p.7). Distances errors are 16%/84% Gaia DR3 (Table 1).",
 "conventions": {
  "pa": "degrees East of North (Table 3 header)",
  "separation": "projected, milliarcseconds",
  "band": "H (~1.6 micron), MIRC-X R~190 grism; HD 31647 also observed in K with MYSTIC (R50 prism) in 2021 Oct 21 (no companion detected)",
  "observing_nights": "UT 2020 Dec 20-21 (26 stars); HD 31647 on UT 2021 Oct 21",
